Our platform layer's mixer (rom/gen3/wasm/layer) takes the place of m4a_1.s. Under IRV_WASM
m4a.c runs it at 42048 Hz, the highest rate of the expansion's table: 704 samples per frame
at 59.7275 frames per second, which the page resamples. The rest of m4a.c stays as it is: the
layer's PSG reads the registers that CgbSound and CgbOscOff write.

diff --git a/src/m4a.c b/src/m4a.c
--- a/src/m4a.c
+++ b/src/m4a.c
@@ -73,7 +73,11 @@
     SoundInit(&gSoundInfo);
     MPlayExtender(gCgbChans);
     m4aSoundMode(SOUND_MODE_DA_BIT_8
+#ifdef IRV_WASM
+               | SOUND_MODE_FREQ_42048
+#else
                | SOUND_MODE_FREQ_13379
+#endif
                | (12 << SOUND_MODE_MASVOL_SHIFT)
                | (5 << SOUND_MODE_MAXCHN_SHIFT));
 
